---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Let’s talk"
  description="Talk to Tom about a bespoke application, connected quality control or an SAP Business One and Produmex integration."
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap contact-intro">
    <p class="section-note">Let’s talk</p>
    <h1>
      What’s missing from
      <br />
      your business software?
    </h1>
    <p class="page-lead">
      Tell me where the process gets awkward, what you use today, and what a
      better way of working would look like.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a
        class="button"
        href="mailto:tom@outerjoin.be?subject=Let%27s%20discuss%20a%20workflow"
      >
        Email Tom <Icon />
      </a>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tbernaerd"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Connect on LinkedIn <Icon />
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="contact-email">
      <a href="mailto:tom@outerjoin.be">tom@outerjoin.be</a>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section studio-section">
    <div class="wrap contact-grid">
      <div class="contact-person">
        <img
          src="/tom-bernaerd.jpg"
          alt="Tom Bernaerd"
          width="110"
          height="110"
        />
        <div>
          <h2>Tom Bernaerd</h2>
          <p>Outer Join · Belgium</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A useful first conversation.</h2>
        <p>
          We’ll look at the workflow, the systems involved and where an
          application could help. From there, we can agree whether a walkthrough
          or a scoped discovery is the right next step.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can start with a simple description. A specification can come
          later.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
